        <field name="name">Starting on My Day</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p><span class="oe-path">My Day</span> is a start screen for the day: today's meetings, to-dos, calls and texts to answer, tickets, leads, tasks, money owed to you and money due, and quotes waiting on customers, each with a link to the full list.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/business_elearning/static/img/my_day.png" alt="My Day with today's schedule, a voicemail, a text to answer, leads and a task due" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>a print shop's My Day on the Meadow background: a proof review, a voicemail and a text to answer, two leads and a task due tomorrow.</p></div><p>To open it every time you log in, tick <strong>Start on My Day</strong> in your <span class="oe-path">Preferences</span> (your picture, top right). Everything on it is yours: other people see their own day.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-lightbulb-o" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Work from the top</span><p>Plan with the left column (schedule and to-dos), then clear the right column (what needs attention) between meetings.</p></div></div><p><strong>Leads</strong> shows your open leads, the ones with a next step due first, then new leads in your sales team that nobody has picked up yet: <span class="oe-path">Take</span> makes one yours. <strong>Texts</strong> works the same way for messages to the business's numbers: take one, <span class="oe-path">Reply</span>, or mark it <span class="oe-path">Done</span>.</p><p>Whoever looks after security also sees <strong>Threat status</strong>: green when all is clear, amber when there's something to review, red when it needs you now.</p><p>Make it yours with the picture button at the top: pick a background, or upload your own photo.</p></div></field>
    </record>
