    <record id="channel_sales_s2_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_sales" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Quotes customers sign and pay online</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">23</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>From an opportunity, <span class="oe-path">New Quotation</span> starts a quote for that customer. Add the products, then <span class="oe-path">Send by Email</span>. The customer opens a link, reads the quote, signs it and pays the deposit right there.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/business_elearning/static/img/quote_portal.png" alt="A quote as the customer sees it, with a Sign &amp; Pay button" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>what the customer sees: the quote, a 50% down payment and Sign &amp; Pay.</p></div><p>Switch it on once in <span class="oe-path">Sales › Configuration › Settings</span>: <strong>Online Signature</strong> and <strong>Online Payment</strong> (with the deposit percentage). Payments need a payment provider, set up in <span class="oe-path">Accounting › Configuration › Online Payments › Payment Providers</span>.</p><div class="oe-callout oe-callout-success"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-check" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Signed and paid</span><p>When the customer signs and pays, the quote becomes a confirmed sales order on its own, and the payment is recorded.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
